From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ps5cemu <ps5cemu@localhost>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 12:06:04 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] PS5: the GPU thread waits for commands without yielding, with
 idle spinning

When the GPU thread runs out of commands it spins 80 PAUSEs, looks at
its timers and yields, round and round. On the PS5 a yield is a call into
the kernel, and while every CPU is busy (pipelines compiling as a game
streams an area in) it can give the thread's CPU to another thread for a
whole time slice, so the next commands the emulated CPU writes wait for
it. With the port's idle spinning on (g_ps5IdleSpinIterations, the same
experiment as the idle cores'), the wait spins without yielding.
---
 src/Cafe/HW/Latte/Core/LatteCommandProcessor.cpp | 14 ++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 14 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/Cafe/HW/Latte/Core/LatteCommandProcessor.cpp b/src/Cafe/HW/Latte/Core/LatteCommandProcessor.cpp
index de67772..1a48877 100644
--- a/src/Cafe/HW/Latte/Core/LatteCommandProcessor.cpp
+++ b/src/Cafe/HW/Latte/Core/LatteCommandProcessor.cpp
@@ -8,6 +8,14 @@
 #include "Cafe/HW/Latte/Core/LattePerformanceMonitor.h"
 #include "Cafe/HW/Latte/Core/LatteIndices.h"
 #include "Cafe/HW/Latte/Core/LatteBufferCache.h"
+#if defined(CEMU_PS5)
+// PS5: the port's idle spinning (coreinit_Thread.cpp), which the GPU thread's wait for commands
+// follows too
+namespace coreinit
+{
+	extern uint32 g_ps5IdleSpinIterations;
+}
+#endif
 #include "Cafe/HW/Latte/Core/LattePM4.h"
 #include "Cafe/HW/Latte/Core/LatteSurfaceCopy.h"
 
@@ -191,6 +199,12 @@ uint32 LatteCP_readU32Deprc()
 		// still no command data available, do some other tasks
 		LatteTiming_HandleTimedVsync();
 		LatteAsyncCommands_checkAndExecute();
+#if defined(CEMU_PS5)
+		// PS5: with idle spinning on, no yield: on the console it is a call into the kernel, and while
+		// every CPU is busy (pipelines compiling) it can give this thread's CPU away for a whole time
+		// slice, so the next commands wait. The 80 PAUSEs above keep the wait polite.
+		if (coreinit::g_ps5IdleSpinIterations == 0)
+#endif
 		std::this_thread::yield();
 		performanceMonitor.gpuTime_idleTime.endMeasuring();
 	}
